Attempt 1: accuracy=71.0% syntax=74.0% (n=100)
  Helpers: unconstrained=UnconstrainedStep (token-by-token); delimiter-triggered << entry; constrained=AdaptiveConstrainedStep; explicit close on IsCompletePrefix
  Rationale: Math-step CSD with delimiter-triggered constrained arithmetic spans.
The strategy tracks the usual generation state (`generated`), whether we are
currently inside a `<< ... >>` constrained region, and the current contents
of that region (`currentConstrainedOut`). Inside a constrained span it also
uses the caller-provided `validTokenGroups` as soft preferences for tokens
that are useful in arithmetic expressions, via an adaptive constrained
sampler.
Action choice is driven by three observations: outside a span we generate
freely so the model can write natural language reasoning; when the token
`"<<"` appears we enter constrained mode with an empty arithmetic prefix;
while inside the span, if the parser says the arithmetic prefix is complete
we close with `">>"`, otherwise we sample the next token from the parser-
valid set, softly boosted by `validTokenGroups` when the grammar is narrow.
This state supports valid generation because `currentConstrainedOut` always
mirrors exactly the suffix of `generated` between delimiters, so parser-valid
updates can be appended to both simultaneously. The parser therefore governs
every token written inside `<< >>`, ensuring arithmetic computations are
emitted as valid constrained spans while leaving explanatory text outside the
delimiters unconstrained.

*** Best so far: attempt 1 (71.0% accuracy)
